/*!
\page page_sthlttriggerreasoncapable StHltTriggerReasonCapable

\brief Abstract marker base class for HLT physics objects that can serve as the reason for an online trigger decision.

\section overview Overview

`StHltTriggerReasonCapable` is an abstract base class (marker interface) that tags HLT physics
objects as capable of serving as a trigger reason. By inheriting from this class,
\ref StHltHighPt, \ref StHltHeavyFragment, \ref StHltDiElectron, and \ref StHltTrackNode can all
be pointed to polymorphically by \ref StHltTriggerReason via its `mReason` link. This design
allows trigger-reason code to operate through a single base-class pointer regardless of the
concrete trigger type.

The class adds no data members or methods beyond `StObject`. Its role is purely to provide a
common base type for polymorphic dispatch in the HLT trigger-reason chain.

\section hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject
└── StObject
    └── StHltTriggerReasonCapable
        ├── StHltHighPt
        ├── StHltHeavyFragment
        ├── StHltDiElectron
        └── StHltTrackNode
\endcode

\section datamembers Data Members

None beyond those inherited from `StObject`.

\section keymethods Key Methods

None beyond those inherited from `StObject`.

\section example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
// Downcast from StHltTriggerReasonCapable* using reasonBit() to determine concrete type:
StHltTriggerReasonCapable* obj = tr->reason();
if (tr->reasonBit() == kHighPt) {
    const StHltHighPt* hp = static_cast<const StHltHighPt*>(obj);
    // use hp ...
}
\endcode

\see StHltTriggerReason
\see StHltHighPt
\see StHltHeavyFragment
\see StHltDiElectron
\see StHltTrackNode
*/
